<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The small icon of the drive notification (位置情報を使用中), shown in the
  status bar and in the notification shade for as long as a drive runs.

  Android draws a status bar icon from its alpha channel only, so this is a
  white silhouette on a transparent ground: 24dp, on a 24-unit viewport.

  THE SHAPE IS A ROAD, AND IT IS DELIBERATELY NOT A LOCATION MARK. While any
  app uses location, Android draws its own location indicator in the same
  status bar. This icon used to be the location crosshair (Icons.my_location).
  Seen on an Android 14 emulator with another app still using location: one
  second after 停止, this app's icon was gone and Android's location pin
  stayed. A driver who had learned "the location mark is my drive" could take
  that pin for her drive, and its warnings, still running. A road is not a
  location mark, it is not one of Android's status icons, and it is present
  only while her drive is. test/drive_notification_icon_not_location_test.dart
  fails if this shape is ever a location glyph again.

  It is not a snowflake or a warning triangle on purpose: inside the app those
  two mean "the road may be frozen" and "a caution is raised", and an icon
  shown for every drive would claim them on every drive.

  Two edges converging on the horizon, and a centre line of three dashes
  that narrow with distance. Each piece is a separate filled shape; none
  overlap, so no fill rule is needed.

  Drawn for this app; derived from no font glyph or icon set. Licensed with
  the rest of this repository (BSD 3-Clause, see LICENSE).

  geolocator finds this drawable by name at run time, so nothing in the APK
  refers to it; res/raw/keep.xml keeps it through release resource shrinking.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">
    <!-- left edge -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:pathData="M8.4,2.5 L10.4,2.5 L6.2,21.5 L2.2,21.5 Z" />
    <!-- right edge -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:pathData="M13.6,2.5 L15.6,2.5 L21.8,21.5 L17.8,21.5 Z" />
    <!-- centre line: near, middle and far dash -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:pathData="M10.75,15.2 L13.25,15.2 L13.25,21.5 L10.75,21.5 Z M11.1,8.6 L12.9,8.6 L12.9,12.9 L11.1,12.9 Z M11.5,3.0 L12.5,3.0 L12.5,6.4 L11.5,6.4 Z" />
</vector>
